SUMMARY:Free Screening // Citizen Minutes: Series 1 & 2
DESCRIPTION:In honour of Citizenship Week\, we screening 15 short documentaries highlighting ordinary Canadians doing extraordinary things to improve their communities. \nAt a time when citizen engagement is needed more than ever\, these short doc collections\, commissioned by Hot Docs\, showcase Canadians who are making extraordinary impacts in their communities. Our mission is to inspire engagement in Canadian democracy by celebrating stories of civic participation across the country. \nMore about the films & the project: citizenminutes.ca \nTickets: FREE \nFilms in the Citizen Minutes collection are commissioned by Hot Docs. The Citizen Minutes project is made possible through support by The Rossy Foundation.
URL:https://nowtoronto.com/event/free-screening-citizen-minutes-series-1-2/
LOCATION:Hot Docs Ted Rogers Cinema\, 506 Bloor Street West\, Toronto\, M5S 1Y3
CATEGORIES:Film & Media
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://nowtoronto.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/free-screening-citizen-minutes-series-1-2.png
END:VEVENT
