SUMMARY:The Collective of Cool Cats: Jazz-Classical from Beyond the Iron
DESCRIPTION:It’s likely that the former Soviet Union is not what comes to mind when you think of American Jazz\, this concert will change that. \nJazz had a rocky relationship with the powers that were\, often denounced as counter-revolutionary American bourgeoise decadence. It was even effectively banned alongside saxophones between 1949 to 1953\, with several key figures in the scene jailed or exiled. Despite it all\, the syncopated rhythms\, flashy improvised solos\, and nasty chords of jazz managed to inspire musicians and listeners all over Eastern Europe and West\, Central and East Asia. \nFeaturing Nikolai Kapustin’s Viola Sonata & the Canadian premiere of Yuri Chugunov’s Suite of Moods for Alto Sax and Piano; as well as groovy pieces by Alexander Tsfasman\, Arno Babajanian\, Vagif Mustafazadeh\, Andrei Eshpai and more. \nPerformers include:Wallace Halladay (Saxophone)Ivan Estey Jovanovic (Piano)and The Ezra Duo – Jacob Clewell (viola/violin) and Sasha Bult-Ito (piano) \nFriday\, April 17th7:00pmHeliconian Hall\, Toronto \nTickets: $20/$30
URL:https://nowtoronto.com/event/the-collective-of-cool-cats-jazz-classical-from-beyond-the-iron/
LOCATION:Heliconian Club\, 35 Hazelton Ave\, Toronto\, ON M5R 2E3\, Canada\, Old Toronto\, Toronto\, Ontario\, M5R 2E3
CATEGORIES:History & Heritage,Live Music,Performing Arts
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://nowtoronto.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/the-collective-of-cool-cats-jazz-classical-from-beyond-the-iron.png
END:VEVENT
